<title>RUSSIA: SAS begins Stockholm-Arkhangelsk route.</title>
<headline>SAS begins Stockholm-Arkhangelsk route.</headline>
<dateline>ST PETERSBURG 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines (SAS) has started regular passenger flights between Stockholm and the northern Russian city of Arkhangelsk, a company official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>District manager Marek Pederson said SAS was running regular flights three times a week on a 110-seat McDonell Douglas MD-87 jet.</p>
<p>Arkhangelsk is the fourth Russian city, after Moscow, St Petersburg and Kaliningrad, to which SAS makes regular flights. SAS is the first Western carrier to fly to Arkhangelsk.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
